      "content": "The standard approach for your scenario involves calculating a safety stock buffer using the formula: Safety Stock = Z-score × √(Lead Time Variance × Average Demand² + Average Demand² × Lead Time Variance). This formula explicitly accounts for variability in both average demand and lead time, which is crucial for unstable supply chains like Shenzhen components. Once you determine your desired service level to define the Z-score, you can add this calculated buffer to your regular reorder point to prevent stockouts during peak seasons.",
